--- body ---

## Context

0816 established a useful availability diagnostic, not a portfolio finding:
the inspected cases do not currently provide a complete operation-level join of
transition function, strict finance evidence and genuine dated history. Its
second review found a small set of semantic and reproducibility defects. Astra
recommends this bounded repair, followed immediately by 0817; do not redesign
the protocol or build a universal validator.

## First test

Add a failing fixture in which a mixed, source-linked financing observation
(Saguling) supports B, a South African register entry cannot be promoted to a
signed financial state, and the derived summary rejects duplicate IDs or a
`supports_B_strict=yes` row without a finance observation.

## Actions

Correct the eight source-linked rows and their report so that every field is
faithful to its evidence. Add the minimal consistency assertions needed to
derive counts from the reviewed CSV. State plainly that the CSV is a manually
coded, source-reviewed diagnostic and that the script reproduces its summary,
not an automatic reconstruction of histories. Complete only the collection
vocabulary required by 0817: allocation, disbursement, duplicate, unavailable
and lost visibility. Preserve `announced` as the explicit pledge equivalent if
used. Do not make a before/after history a paper inclusion criterion.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Saguling has its existing mixed, unallocated finance observation and no private-share inference
- [ ] ZAF register-derived entries are not labelled signed without signature evidence
- [ ] Summary counts are generated from rows and reject incompatible flags or duplicate identities
- [ ] Report makes no claim that the matrix or histories are automatically reconstructed
- [ ] Lifecycle and source-disposition vocabulary is sufficient for the 0817 census
- [ ] 0817 can use the repaired diagnostic as a limited source lead, not as a four-country result

